        "display": "tell",
        "explain": "The result can be an instruction: the imperative ‘tell’, with no subject."
      },
      {
        "use": "Unless",
        "before": "Unless you",
        "after": "now, you’ll be late.",
        "hint": "(leave)",
        "answers": [
          "leave"
        ],
        "display": "leave",
        "explain": "‘Unless’ means ‘if not’, so the verb after it is affirmative: ‘unless you leave’."
      },
      {
        "use": "Time linker",
        "before": "I’ll text you as soon as I",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(arrive)",
        "answers": [
          "arrive"
        ],
        "display": "arrive",
        "explain": "After ‘as soon as’ (like ‘if’) use the present simple for the future."
      }
